From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cam_smmu: fix mainline iommu warn and coherency probe race

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [adapts downstream camx-dlkm to a mainline kernel]

Two issues when the camera_kt SMMU code runs on a mainline (linux-yocto)
kernel instead of the downstream vendor kernel:

1. cam_populate_smmu_context_banks() sets a fault handler on the context
   bank's domain obtained from iommu_get_domain_for_dev(), which on mainline
   is the default managed (DMA) domain. iommu_set_fault_handler() rejects a
   managed domain with WARN_ON(cookie_type != IOMMU_COOKIE_NONE) and returns
   without installing the handler - so it is already a no-op, it just floods
   the log with one backtrace per context bank at probe. Only install the
   handler on an unmanaged domain.

2. cam_smmu_need_force_alloc_cached() validates coherency across cb_num (all
   allocated context banks) but is reached from cam_mem_mgr_init() on the
   first cam_req_mgr open, which can happen before every context bank has been
   populated during boot. An unpopulated bank has a NULL name and the default
   CAM_SMMU_NO_COHERENCY, so with force_cache_allocs set it fails with
   "[(null)] Can't force alloc cache with no coherency", mem mgr init fails
   and the first ICP FW download fails until a later retry. Validate only the
   populated banks (cb_init_count); all camera banks are dma-coherent so the
   result is unchanged once every bank is bound.

Signed-off-by: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
---
 camera_kt/drivers/cam_smmu/cam_smmu_api.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/camera_kt/drivers/cam_smmu/cam_smmu_api.c b/camera_kt/drivers/cam_smmu/cam_smmu_api.c
--- a/camera_kt/drivers/cam_smmu/cam_smmu_api.c
+++ b/camera_kt/drivers/cam_smmu/cam_smmu_api.c
@@ -389,7 +389,7 @@
 	 * This helps as a validation check to make sure a valid DT combination
 	 * is set for a given chipset.
 	 */
-	for (idx = 0; idx < iommu_cb_set.cb_num; idx++) {
+	for (idx = 0; idx < iommu_cb_set.cb_init_count; idx++) {
 		/* ignore secure cb for now. need to revisit */
 		if (iommu_cb_set.cb_info[idx].is_secure)
 			continue;
@@ -4013,7 +4013,8 @@
 		rc= PTR_ERR(cb->domain);
 		goto cb_init_fail;
 	}
-	if (cb->io_support && cb->domain)
+	if (cb->io_support && cb->domain &&
+		cb->domain->type == IOMMU_DOMAIN_UNMANAGED)
 		iommu_set_fault_handler(cb->domain,
 			cam_smmu_iommu_fault_handler,
 			(void *)cb->name[0]);
